THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL

  Libraries bundled into the site (three.js, jsPDF and what it bundles,
  Lucide icons, ONNX Runtime Web): app/public/third-party-notices.txt and
  app/public/onnxruntime-third-party-notices.txt, which ship with the
  site.

  Sample models and pictures in app/public/samples/: each keeps its own
  licence (CC0, CC BY 4.0, or public domain), listed with its source in
  app/public/samples/README.md and on the site's About page.

  Data: which parts were made in which colours, and what is in each set,
  comes from Rebrickable's data downloads (each JSON file in app/src/data/
  and app/public/data/ names its source). Part numbers and colour values follow
  the LDraw.org parts library and LDConfig.ldr (CC BY 2.0 / CC BY 4.0).
  No LDraw part geometry is stored here.

  Depth model: the mosaic's 2.5D option downloads Depth Anything V2 Small
  (Apache-2.0) from Hugging Face at run time; it is not stored here.


WORK THIS PROJECT BUILDS ON

  - app/src/convert/slopes.mjs follows the slope-profile rule of
    legolization by Harold Martin (https://github.com/hbmartin/legolization,
    GPL-3.0-or-later), rewritten in JavaScript with different data structures.
    AGPL-3.0 section 13 allows combining this project with GPL-3.0 work.
  - "Match a picture to a fixed set of parts" (app/src/mosaic/stock.mjs)
    and the 2.5D mosaic idea (app/src/mosaic/relief.mjs) come from
    lego-art-remix by Deb Banerji
    (https://github.com/debkbanerji/lego-art-remix, GPL-3.0); the code
    here was written separately.
  - Rejoining loose parts (app/src/convert/repair.mjs) takes its idea from
    Brickify by Adrian Sieber
    (https://github.com/ad-si/Brickify, AGPL-3.0-or-later); no code from
    it is used.
  - Papers: M. Agrawala et al., "Designing Effective Step-By-Step Assembly
    Instructions", SIGGRAPH 2003 (building steps); R. Ramamoorthi and
    P. Hanrahan, "An Efficient Representation for Irradiance Environment
    Maps", SIGGRAPH 2001 (removing baked lighting); G. Sharma, W. Wu and
    E. N. Dalal, "The CIEDE2000 Color-Difference Formula", 2005;
    B. Ottosson, "A perceptual color space for image processing" (OKLab),
    2020; R. W. Floyd and L. Steinberg, "An Adaptive Algorithm for
    Spatial Greyscale", 1976 (dithering).
